Blend the shine of a background over the window

The window background paints in the replacing composition mode of the
caller. The shine highlight of a gradient border takes the same mode, so
the white pixmap of the shine replaces the background below it. The
pixmap also carries its own alpha into the window. The outer stop of the
shine holds the alpha zero, so a black rim stands where the highlight
ends. The whole region ignores the background opacity as well, because
the alpha of the pixmap replaces the alpha of the window.

The shine now blends over the painted background in the mode that keeps
the alpha of the destination. The highlight therefore lightens the
background, and it follows the opacity of the window. A gradient border
without a shine reaches no line of this path.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 7 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
